{{Quote|Sector One, alert. Enemy gunship approaching your location. Come in, Sector One.|A battle droid alerting Separatist forces in Sector One|<ref name="Bad Batch" />}}
'''Sector One''' was a location on<ref name="Bad Batch" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|fort-anaxes|Fort Anaxes}}</ref> [[Anaxes]], utilized by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance's]] [[Separatist Droid Army|droid army]] during the [[Clone Wars]]' [[Battle of Anaxes]]<ref name="Bad Batch" /> in [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> During the battle, a [[Galactic Republic]] [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] [[gunship]] traveled near Sector One, carrying [[Clone Force 99]], [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody]], [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], [[Advanced Recon Commando]] [[Jesse]], and [[Kix]].<ref name="Bad Batch" />

However, the [[trooper]]s were spotted by a Separatist [[B1-series battle droid|battle droid]] [[scout]] that alerted an [[OOM command battle droid]] and a [[Unidentified droid battalion (Anaxes)|droid battalion]] stationed in Sector One about the incoming Republic [[Starship|vessel]]. [[Confederacy military|Separatist forces]] subsequently shot down the gunship in a nearby canyon using [[DSD1 dwarf spider droid]]s. In the canyon, the [[Cloning|clone]] troopers were briefly engaged by the [[droid]] [[battalion]], resulting in the ship's destruction. Afterward, the clone troopers pressed forward on their mission to infiltrate a Separatist [[Cyber Center]] despite being shot down.<ref name="Bad Batch" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:TCW_Sector_one.png|thumb|right|250px|Sector One, as it appears in the Bad Batch story reels]]
Sector One was introduced in "[[The Bad Batch (episode)|The Bad Batch]],"<ref name="Bad Batch" /> the first episode of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series' [[The Clone Wars: Season Seven|seventh and final season]], which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[February 21]], [[2020]].<ref name="SW.com final">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-final-season|text=The Final Season of ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Begins!}}</ref> The episode originally aired as an unfinished story reel on [[April 17]], [[2015]], at [[Celebration Anaheim (2015)|Celebration Anaheim]],<ref name="Anaheim Announcement">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-bad-batch-4-episode-arc-coming-to-star-wars-celebration|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' "Bad Batch" 4-Episode Arc Coming to ''Star Wars'' Celebration|nolive=1}}</ref> and later on [[StarWars.com]] on [[April 29]] as part of [[The Clone Wars Legacy|''The Clone Wars'' Legacy]] multimedia project.<ref name="SW.com">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-bad-batch-recon|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' "Bad Batch" Recon|nolive=1}}</ref>

